\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\qc\b\f0\fs40\lang9 IPL Match Analysis (2008\f1\endash\f0 2020) Using Python and Pandas\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b0\f2\fs22\par

\pard{\pntext\f10\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf10\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f3\fs28 Abstract\b0\f2\fs22\par

\pard\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f4 The objective of this project is to analyze IPL match data from 2008 to 2020 using Python libraries such as Pandas, Matplotlib, and Seaborn. The project focuses on extracting meaningful insights from historical IPL match records through statistical analysis and data visualization techniques\f2 .\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par

\pard{\pntext\f10\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf10\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f3\fs28 Introduction\b0\f4\fs22\par

\pard\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 The Indian Premier League (IPL) is one of the most popular cricket tournaments in the world. Every season generates a large amount of match-related data, making it an excellent source for data analysis. This project aims to study team performances, toss decisions, match results, venues, and player achievements using data science techniques.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f2\par

\pard{\pntext\f10\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf10\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f3\fs28 Objectives\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f2\fs22\par

\pard\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\qj\f4 * Perform exploratory data analysis on IPL match data.\par
* Identify the most successful teams.\par
* Analyze toss decisions and match outcomes.\par
* Study player performance through Player of the Match awards.\par
* Visualize important trends using charts and graphs\f2 .\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par

